      ],
      "canonical_claim": "Squirrel Crossing uses one continuous flowing vector through moving traffic, with limited predeclared redirection, potentially one or two redirects, exploiting relative motion and vehicle wakes while accelerating toward a known far-side climbable refuge or vertical anchor. It seeks a moving traffic window rather than fixed micro-features or one broad static opening, and it does not require convenient vertical anchors in the middle of an ordinary highway. Its strengths are direct speed, leap commitment, and infrastructure use.",
      "human_question": null,
      "members": [
